We are essentially being asked for the product of \( x_i^2 - 2 \) over all roots of \( f(x) \). Consider the polynomial whose roots are \( y_i = x_i^2 \). Alternatively, maybe better to consider a function of the roots.

Alternatively, recall that for a monic polynomial \( f(x) = \prod_{i=1}^5 (x - x_i) \), the value of \( \prod_{i} (x - r_i) \) evaluated at a point is just \( f \) evaluated at that point.

But here, it's not quite \( f \) evaluated at something, but rather the product over transformations of the roots.

